+# Capability: rt-03-06-2026-10-09
+
+## Requirement
+- The candidate SHALL validate full immutable byte bindings and preserve original independent CPU oracle tuples before new replay.
+- It SHALL atomically adopt current source generations, retain both BVH and sparse flat/two-level APIs, reject stale source/owner/frame/material/device/epoch results and release rejected/old resources.
+- It SHALL execute provenance-labelled finite synthetic Cut/Fragment/100Edit/origin/save-reset streams; none is an actual gameplay cut or product export. Unknown, budget, empty and invalid source are distinct.
+- A low-resolution caller-owned raster G-buffer SHALL create at most one short ray per eligible pixel, preserve PrimitiveHit metadata, compose linear HDR without double AO and tone map once outside the pass. Existing GFX ports/materials SHALL be reused.
+- History SHALL reject opening/rotation/fragment/teleport/sun/resize/wind/Unknown/source/lifetime changes and perform only an edge-aware bounded filter; no stale light resurrection.
+- The finite runner SHALL validate real compile/query/lifecycle on caller-owned device/depth, compare Shadowmap and screen AO on the same backend, record actual adapter/features/limits/browser/environment, and report unavailable vendor classes. It SHALL require explicit A0 slot and unloaded window for qualification; no GPU execution in producer startup.
+- Complete source/index/staged/unstaged/untracked/fixture/lock/WASM/shader/build/tool bytes SHALL be sealed; exact diff and README/REPORT/HANDOFF/receipt/repro profile SHALL be delivered without commits/pushes/human approval simulation.
+
+## Scenarios
+### Scenario: asynchronous old cut completes after a new source
+- Given primary revision R+1 and a result for R, adoption rejects and disposes the result; lighting uses current primary fallback.
+### Scenario: opening or unknown neighbor
+- Given a current opening or unresolved ray, old occlusion/history is discarded and Unknown is not promoted to confirmed air.
+### Scenario: fragment ownership and motion
+- Given transfer, occupied stable cell IDs have one owner; movement advances transform identity independently of source generation.
+### Scenario: missing hardware timer
+- Given absent timestamp queries or device, GPU milliseconds are null and the relevant status is NOT_RUN/UNSUPPORTED; CPU wall time is diagnostic only.
