+```powershell
+& .\spikes\gfx-03-backend-bakeoff\repro.ps1 -Mode code
+& .\spikes\gfx-03-backend-bakeoff\repro.ps1 -Mode preview
+```
+
+Open `http://127.0.0.1:43103/`. Select one backend and one fixture, then Mount. The lab owns one renderer and one demand-driven draw path; two render stages share one loop (linear half-float HDR, then exactly one ACES/sRGB output). This is an executable diagnostic comparison, not a product or temporal renderer. Only `?testBridge=1` exposes `window.GfxBridge`. No TestBridge exists on `/`.
+
+Hypothesis: bounded TSL ports of actual HVP sky/strata/stationary-water formulas and existing RD14 wetness/owner-local wind can compile without sacrificing required vertex colour/AO/alpha/depth semantics. The browser checks prove functionality and fault sensitivity. Strict old/new-version and WebGL/WebGPU pixel equivalence FAIL; no visual equivalence or adoption is claimed.
