+# RT-01: frozen render/collider inputs and independent CPU ray oracle
+
+Run from this isolated worktree under `C:\IFI_SourceCode`:
+
+```powershell
+& .\spikes\rt-01-oracle\repro.ps1
+```
+
+The finite profile runs strict typecheck, emitted JavaScript build, focused tests, read-only fixture regeneration/parity, and byte-binding verification. It starts no browser, server, native physics pilot or GPU work. No package installation is needed. Node 22.23.2 and the existing TypeScript 7.0.2 compiler are used; `repro.ps1` accepts explicit Node/Compiler paths. Compiler bytes are read from A0's installed dependency; no A0 files or node_modules are changed.
+
+## Hypothesis and reuse
+
+A small DDA adapted from fixed-base `apps/weltraum-browser/src/hestia-prototype/terrain/picking.ts` can agree with an independent exhaustive ray/AABB oracle while preserving Unknown and owner/frame revisions. The original product picker is exercised unchanged by `control.test.mjs`.
+
+F00-CONTROL comes unchanged from R&D commit `04902cef0b3b7129a6069bf945f39f22e414b6f9`. `imported/F00-CONTROL/import-manifest.json` binds original Git blobs, LFS object digests and actual payload bytes. Existing voxel occupancy/known coverage/material slots, 18 mesh buffers and three cameras are reused. The historical native assertions and final Ray/Greedy report are preserved unchanged. RAY02/RAY03 remain historical FAIL; original 4/6 and corrected helper 10/12 are distinct from this new CPU population.
+
+There are eight **ANALYTICAL** snapshots and one **RD_SYNTHETIC** snapshot. No genuine PRODUCT_EXPORT is present or claimed. Cut, transfer, movement and origin shift are explicitly synthetic snapshot replay; they are not newly executed player flows. The analytical collider exporter emits occupied-cell AABBs; it is not a terrain compiler. Original F00 mesh bytes are the render input.
+
+## Frozen contract
+
+`../_shared/rt-2026-10-09/v1/manifest.json` lists 49 payload files with SHA256, plus the manifest itself. Its digest is `bc6e9be728c932b0fe6f88ea2d6024f61b2b53bc59d47aae0e941c499a34dbea`. Consumers read v1 or a digest-bound copy. `export.mjs --verify` only reads/regenerates in memory. `--freeze-v1` fails if v1 already exists; revised fixture bytes require a new version.
+
+`voxels/*.json` are x-fastest arrays (`x + sx*(y + sy*z)`): -1 Unknown, 0 KnownEmpty, positive canonical material ID. Binary bytes use 255 Unknown, 0 KnownEmpty and positive material slots. Sizes are bounded to 64 per axis. Authority leaves remain 16 cells; these ray pages are 8 cells. The 18-cell analytical X range crosses page and authority-leaf boundaries at negative metric origins and supports 0.125/0.25 m cells.
+
+Binding includes domain/world/session/epoch, owner and source revision/generation/digest, material profile digest, frame/origin epoch, transform generation and algorithm. Source digest covers cell size/origin/full coverage/cells/IDs/page layout and excludes rotation/translation; movement updates transform generation. Current binding comes from the consumer, never from delayed work. `loadFrozenVolume(id, trustedManifestDigest, currentBinding)` verifies bytes and source/material digests and returns a recursively frozen copy.
+
+## Ray policy
+
+Rays are normalized metric rays and use `[0,maxDistance)`. Only intervals longer than `1e-10 * max(1,abs(entry),abs(exit))` count as visited cells. A zero-length/tangent contact is ignored. Near-face representational roundoff is at most eight machine epsilons, capped at `cellWidth * 1e-6`; this does not use the larger time tolerance to change ownership.
+
+Cells are direction-owned on exact faces: negative directions select the preceding cell; a zero component uses min-inclusive/max-exclusive bounds. Starting in an occupied cell, including a direction-owned face, returns distance 0 and zero normal. Entry from outside returns the first crossed face normal. Simultaneous axes advance together; one normal is reported in X/Y/Z priority. Normals are transformed by the orthonormal owner frame; distances remain meters.
+
+`maxSteps` counts positive-length cell intervals per volume. Exhaustion with another such cell yields BudgetExceeded at that cell, never Miss. Unknown inside coverage stops traversal before a farther Hit. Analytical finite-volume exterior is explicitly KnownEmpty; the R&D crop exterior is Unknown, including rays starting outside it. Unknown exterior has no invented surface normal or cell ID. A sub-tolerance excess past maxDistance does not create an exterior Unknown interval.
+
+`rays/golden-1000.json` contains 1000 unique deterministic numeric rays, independent AABB expectations, current bindings and four distinct outcomes. Separate explicit edge tests cover zero components, inside/face/corner starts, simultaneous crossings, budget end, negative coordinates, rotation, origin switch, missing neighbor and stale bindings.
+
+## Delivery and limits
+
+`REPORT.md`, `HANDOFF.md`, `receipt.json`, `binding-manifest.json` and own Spec tests record actual exits. The seal binds every Git-dirty file, staged blob identities, ignored compiled output and use-time Node/Git/compiler/product-control bytes. It normalizes only two self-referential receipt digest fields and excludes the envelope itself. Ignored negative-test copies are not source/consumer inputs.
+
+Execution is LOCAL_WINDOWS_ISOLATED CPU functionality under concurrent sessions. Browser/ActualAdapter/GPU timer/reference-device/cross-device/performance/visual quality are NOT_RUN and have no fabricated zero measurements. WASM and shaders are absent from this CPU spike. Product integration is NO; A0 alone may adopt. The inherited DevToolbox product typecheck fails because this worktree has no product node_modules; scope-specific build/tests are recorded separately.
