+The normal UI's mountExperiment wrapper already disposed the outer handle, so it masked the direct factory route. Report-local native-abort.html calls the unchanged actual factory interface directly. `ray-abort-red-02` reproduces the visible ready-host defect on candidate-abort-red-03: abort leaves terminal.disposed=false and the canvas visible even though the base host is aborted. Before-init and during-init controls pass separately. The preceding ray-abort-red-01 failed Chromium spawn with sandbox EPERM before native execution and remains an invocation log, not a native RED.
