+CPU policy remains the RT01 1e-9 comparison and its separate machine-roundoff/1e-10 interval rules. GPU FP32 uses exact directional ownership after RT01 boundary canonicalization; a nonboundary input that collapses to an integer face in FP32 is explicitly Unsupported. The runner checks discrete identities exactly and distance/normal within an experimental 1e-5 tolerance; this is no owner-approved GPU threshold. Actual compile/conformance is **NOT_RUN**.
